dialogue trust_knight_5
title: Before the hold
trigger: Trust knight level=5
once
speaker commander $commander
speaker hero $with

node open commander
  The Knight has a chisel and a mallet out beside the fire. The shield lies face down, and the old line of hold script on the rim has a fresh scrape under it, as if a second line has been started and stopped.
  * You kept the oath. Hold, not hall. I can see it in how you fight. -> people_kept
    if: FlagSet knight:oath_people
    do: AddTrust $with 5
  * You said you'd carry it until you knew. Do you know now? -> kept_kept
    if: FlagSet knight:oath_kept
    do: AddTrust $with 5
  * I told you to scratch it out. You didn't. You were right not to. -> cut_kept
    if: FlagSet knight:oath_cut
    do: AddTrust $with 7
  * That's a new line. -> new_line
    do: AddTrust $with 3

node people_kept hero
  Hold, not hall. I've said it to myself every morning since. It's the only reason I could stand to look at the Captain across a field. Sit down.
  -> line

node kept_kept hero
  I think I do. It took a long road to point anywhere, but it points. Sit down.
  -> line

node cut_kept hero
  I know. You said it to me straight, and I was angry, and then I kept the words anyway, partly to spite you. It turned out spite holds iron as well as faith does. Sit down.
  -> line

node new_line hero
  It's meant to be. I can't get past the first word. Sit down.
  -> line

node line hero
  The old line says stand before the hold. I swore it to people I'd die for. Then I followed this wagon off the ice, and the people I'd die for got bigger. I don't know how to cut that into iron.
  -> sister

node sister commander
  The Knight's hand goes to the strap, where the folded letter still rides flat against the iron.
  * I promised we'd go to her first. That hasn't moved an inch, whatever else has. -> promised_kept
    if: FlagSet knight:sister_promised
    do: AddTrust $with 9
    do: SetFlag knight:thread_home
  * You sent the warning on the next cart. Did anything ever come back? -> warned_kept
    if: FlagSet knight:sister_warned
    do: AddTrust $with 8
    do: SetFlag knight:thread_warned
  * I wouldn't turn the wagon for one hold. I was wrong. It was never one hold. -> denied_mended
    if: FlagSet knight:sister_denied
    do: AddTrust $with 10
    do: SetFlag knight:thread_mended
  * Wherever she is, she knows you're still standing. -> standing
    do: AddTrust $with 6
    do: SetFlag knight:thread_standing

node promised_kept hero
  I know it hasn't. I've watched you keep every other promise on this road, and I've stopped counting the days till the holds. Nobody in a hall ever kept anything for me.
  -> ask

node warned_kept hero
  One line, scratched on the back of my own letter. Not leaving. Hiding the spears in the well. Too stubborn to run and smart enough to make the levy short a few. That's her.
  -> ask

node denied_mended hero
  No. It never was. You saying so now is worth more than the detour would have been. I mean that.
  -> ask

node standing hero
  Still standing. Yes. That's what I'd want her to know, more than anything. That's what the shield's for.
  -> ask

node ask hero
  So. The second line. I've thought of a hundred words for it and none of them fit. You're the one I stand in front of now, Commander. You pick.
  * Stand beside the ones who stand. -> beside
    do: AddTrust $with 8
    do: SetFlag knight:line_beside
  * Stand before the road, and the road holds. -> road
    do: AddTrust $with 5
    do: SetFlag knight:line_road
  * Leave it blank. You've earned not swearing anything to anyone. -> blank
    do: AddTrust $with -2
    do: SetFlag knight:line_blank
  * Cut it later. Tonight, let me take the watch, the way you took it for us at the ford. -> watch
    if: FlagSet founding:watch_knight
    do: AddTrust $with 10
    do: SetFlag knight:line_watch

node beside hero
  Beside. Not in front. Huh. A squire would never say that. I think I'm done being a squire. Hold the lamp, and I'll cut it now.

node road hero
  The road holds. That's the hold's way of saying it, just longer. It'll fit on the rim. I'll cut it small and neat, the way my teacher did.

node blank hero
  Blank. No. A knight without a line is just someone holding iron. I'll leave it for now, since you asked. But I'll fill it in someday, Commander, and it'll be about you whether you like it or not.

node watch hero
  You. Taking the watch. Nobody's ever stood in front of me. I don't think I know how to sleep behind somebody. I'll try. Wake me if anything comes over the ridge.
